# Body motion service — used by robot_server.py to drive the body/arm servos.
#
# Build this into a catkin package (default name: ainex_demo) on the Pi:
#   1. Copy this file to  <ws>/src/ainex_demo/srv/BodyCommand.srv
#   2. In that package's CMakeLists.txt add BodyCommand.srv to add_service_files()
#      and ensure generate_messages() + message_generation/std_msgs deps are set.
#   3. catkin_make && source devel/setup.bash
#
# Request: a JSON-encoded list of [pulse_dict, duration_ms] frames, plus an
# optional global_duration (ms). If global_duration > 0 it overrides every
# frame's per-pulse duration. The service blocks until the whole sequence has
# played, so callers never overlap motor commands.
string commands_json
float64 global_duration
---
bool success
float64 duration_ms
